That's a lot of electricity for

290
00:08:09,996 --> 00:08:11,776
something that sometimes forgets why

291
00:08:11,816 --> 00:08:13,326
you opened the refrigerator.

292
00:08:13,605 --> 00:08:15,425
Now imagine making your brain work even

293
00:08:15,465 --> 00:08:17,235
more efficiently and intensely.

294
00:08:17,511 --> 00:08:19,511
Your body still needs oxygen, glucose,

295
00:08:19,551 --> 00:08:21,191
blood flow, and the right balance of

296
00:08:21,231 --> 00:08:23,261
chemicals to keep everything functioning.

297
00:08:23,439 --> 00:08:24,319
You can't just turn your brain

298
00:08:24,359 --> 00:08:25,779
into a supercomputer and expect

299
00:08:25,819 --> 00:08:27,289
your body to keep up.

300
00:08:27,456 --> 00:08:29,256
You might need more energy, better sleep,

301
00:08:29,296 --> 00:08:30,496
and plenty of recovery.

302
00:08:30,602 --> 00:08:32,462
And no, drinking seventeen energy drinks

303
00:08:32,502 --> 00:08:33,892
won't turn you into Einstein.

304
00:08:34,568 --> 00:08:35,708
It will probably just turn your

305
00:08:35,748 --> 00:08:37,318
heart into a washing machine.

306
00:08:38,250 --> 00:08:39,010
Meanwhile, your girlfriend

307
00:08:39,050 --> 00:08:40,380
sends another message.

308
00:08:41,089 --> 00:08:42,289
"Can we talk?"

309
00:08:42,800 --> 00:08:43,980
Your brain immediately activates

310
00:08:44,020 --> 00:08:45,770
every available resource.

311
00:08:46,037 --> 00:08:46,917
The memory system starts

312
00:08:46,957 --> 00:08:48,507
reviewing your past mistakes.

313
00:08:48,720 --> 00:08:49,820
The emotional system detects

314
00:08:49,860 --> 00:08:51,090
possible danger.

315
00:08:51,364 --> 00:08:52,464
The reasoning system calculates

316
00:08:52,504 --> 00:08:53,814
possible outcomes.

317
00:08:54,061 --> 00:08:55,271
Your body starts sweating.

318
00:08:55,478 --> 00:08:57,238
Your brain is now using more processing

319
00:08:57,278 --> 00:08:59,328
power than a NASA supercomputer.

320
00:08:59,492 --> 00:09:00,394
And all of this…

321
00:09:00,434 --> 00:09:02,104
For a conversation that starts with:

322
00:09:03,050 --> 00:09:04,800
"Why did you like her Instagram picture?"

323
00:09:06,850 --> 00:09:07,630
And here's where things get

324
00:09:07,670 --> 00:09:08,870
really interesting.

325
00:09:08,928 --> 00:09:10,288
What if you literally forced one

326
00:09:10,328 --> 00:09:11,808
hundred percent of your neurons to

327
00:09:11,848 --> 00:09:13,048
fire simultaneously?

328
00:09:13,342 --> 00:09:14,542
Would you become a god?

329
00:09:14,842 --> 00:09:15,955
Absolutely not.

330
00:09:15,995 --> 00:09:17,885
Your brain doesn't work like a light switch.

331
00:09:18,106 --> 00:09:18,926
Different groups of neurons

332
00:09:18,966 --> 00:09:20,566
perform different jobs,

333
00:09:20,606 --> 00:09:22,306
communicating through carefully coordinated

334
00:09:22,346 --> 00:09:24,596
electrical and chemical signals.

335
00:09:25,800 --> 00:09:27,710
Think of your brain as a massive orchestra.

336
00:09:27,938 --> 00:09:29,298
The violin, drums, piano,

337
00:09:29,338 --> 00:09:30,968
and trumpet all have different roles.

338
00:09:31,185 --> 00:09:32,825
Now imagine forcing every musician

339
00:09:32,865 --> 00:09:34,765
to play as loudly as possible at

340
00:09:34,805 --> 00:09:36,315
exactly the same time.

341
00:09:36,430 --> 00:09:37,341
No rhythm.

342
00:09:37,381 --> 00:09:38,581
No coordination.

343
00:09:39,014 --> 00:09:40,009
Just noise.

344
00:09:40,049 --> 00:09:41,249
That's not intelligence.

345
00:09:41,386 --> 00:09:42,586
That's a musical disaster.

346
00:09:43,800 --> 00:09:44,780
In reality, uncontrolled

347
00:09:44,820 --> 00:09:46,860
synchronized electrical activity in

348
00:09:46,900 --> 00:09:48,410
the brain can cause seizures.

349
00:09:48,655 --> 00:09:49,855
So the goal isn't to make every

350
00:09:49,895 --> 00:09:51,305
neuron fire at once.

351
00:09:51,507 --> 00:09:52,547
It's to make the right neurons

352
00:09:52,587 --> 00:09:54,397
communicate at the right time.

353
00:09:55,300 --> 00:09:56,600
And this is exactly what happens

354
00:09:56,640 --> 00:09:57,950
when your girlfriend says:

355
00:09:58,519 --> 00:09:59,504
"We need to talk."

356
00:09:59,544 --> 00:10:00,884
Your memory starts playing every

357
00:10:00,924 --> 00:10:02,894
argument from the last five years.

358
00:10:03,101 --> 00:10:04,561
Your imagination creates seventeen

359
00:10:04,601 --> 00:10:06,371
different disaster scenarios.

360
00:10:06,629 --> 00:10:07,769
Your reasoning tries to identify

361
00:10:07,809 --> 00:10:09,139
what you did wrong.

362
00:10:09,257 --> 00:10:10,927
Your emotional system activates.

363
00:10:11,135 --> 00:10:12,715
And your entire brain becomes one

364
00:10:12,755 --> 00:10:14,505
giant emergency meeting.

365
00:10:14,654 --> 00:10:15,854
All neurons are working.

366
00:10:16,250 --> 00:10:17,450
None of them has a solution.

367
00:10:19,350 --> 00:10:21,010
So, would unlocking one hundred

368
00:10:21,050 --> 00:10:22,390
percent of your brain make you the

369
00:10:22,430 --> 00:10:23,630
smartest human alive?

370
00:10:23,696 --> 00:10:24,838
Not automatically.

371
00:10:24,878 --> 00:10:26,588
Because intelligence isn't a percentage.

372
00:10:26,937 --> 00:10:28,817
It's a combination of memory, learning,

373
00:10:28,857 --> 00:10:30,877
reasoning, creativity, experience,

374
00:10:30,917 --> 00:10:32,017
and how efficiently your brain

375
00:10:32,057 --> 00:10:33,257
uses information.

376
00:10:33,523 --> 00:10:35,513
Einstein didn't need a secret brain switch.

377
00:10:35,725 --> 00:10:36,805
Professional athletes didn't

378
00:10:36,845 --> 00:10:38,415
unlock hidden brain regions.

379
00:10:38,672 --> 00:10:39,492
They developed extraordinary

380
00:10:39,532 --> 00:10:41,252
abilities through practice,

381
00:10:41,292 --> 00:10:42,622
experience, and dedication.

382
00:10:43,800 --> 00:10:45,550
And perhaps the greatest lesson is this:

383
00:10:45,697 --> 00:10:46,597
You might be able to solve

384
00:10:46,637 --> 00:10:48,037
complicated equations,

385
00:10:48,077 --> 00:10:49,297
memorize thousands of books,

386
00:10:49,337 --> 00:10:50,947
predict the movement of a football,

387
00:10:51,017 --> 00:10:51,937
and understand the mysteries

388
00:10:51,977 --> 00:10:53,177
of the universe.

389
00:10:53,286 --> 00:10:54,996
But when your girlfriend says:

390
00:10:55,186 --> 00:10:56,372
"Do whatever you want."

391
00:10:56,412 --> 00:10:57,792
Even a supercomputer might need

392
00:10:57,832 --> 00:10:59,032
professional help.

393
00:10:59,800 --> 00:11:00,780
Because you can study the human

394
00:11:00,820 --> 00:11:02,030
brain for decades.

395
00:11:02,303 --> 00:11:03,653
You can understand the universe.

396
00:11:03,918 --> 00:11:04,958
You can calculate the distance

397
00:11:04,998 --> 00:11:06,198
between galaxies.

398
00:11:06,411 --> 00:11:07,464
But sometimes…

399
00:11:07,504 --> 00:11:08,834
The hardest problem isn't science.

400
00:11:09,843 --> 00:11:11,073
It's deciding where to eat.

401
00:11:11,807 --> 00:11:13,197
See you in the next experiment!
